BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Vermont Maple Conference
DTSTART:20261108T083000
DTEND:20261108T154500
DTSTAMP:20261108T170746Z
UID:041a480e754ee48bbebe28928f84e1@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Vermont’s maple community for three days of learning\, 
 connection\, and hands-on experiences at the 2026 Vermont Maple Conference
 \, presented by the Vermont Maple Sugar Makers’ Association and Universi
 ty of Vermont Extension. This year’s conference brings together maple pr
 oducers\, researchers\, industry professionals\, landowners\, and anyone i
 nterested in maple production for educational programs designed for operat
 ions of all sizes and experience levels. Friday\, November 6 – Maple Qua
 lity School Build your maple quality knowledge through hands-on education 
 focused on producing\, grading\, and maintaining high-quality maple syrup.
  Saturday\, November 7 – Vermont Maple Conference Day Gather for a full 
 day of educational sessions\, industry updates\, research\, practical prod
 uction information\, and opportunities to connect with Vermont’s maple c
 ommunity. Maple Sugarhouse Bus Tours Sunday\, November 8 – Hit the road 
 to visit working Vermont sugarhouses\, meet fellow producers\, and see map
 le production practices\, equipment\, and operations firsthand. Participan
 ts can register for the conference activities that best fit their interest
 s and schedule. Advance registration is encouraged\, and space for some ac
 tivities is limited. Visit VermontMaple.org for schedules\, registration\,
  tour itineraries\, lodging information\, and complete conference details.
 \n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont State University\, 113 Judd Drive
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/2026-vermo
 nt-maple-conference-07-10-2026-17-26-47
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Assassins the Musical
DTSTART:20261108T140000
DTEND:20261108T160000
DTSTAMP:20261108T170746Z
UID:2a2c3f87f556ac3c9b6fba66161656@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Assassins is Stephen Sondheim’s daring\, darkly comic musica
 l that brings together the men and women who attempted—or succeeded—in
  assassinating U.S. presidents. Provocative\, unsettling\, and often distu
 rbingly funny\, the musical challenges audiences to confront the myths of 
 success\, entitlement\, and patriotism at the heart of American culture. T
 his production continues Wild Goose Players’ commitment to live theatre 
 that challenges\, engages\, and invites conversation. 🎭 Content Warning
 : this show has an R-rating and deals with many sensitive topics including
  gun violence\, suicide\, executions\, drug use\, cults/brainwashing and p
 rofanity including a racial slur. Next Stage Arts Every week through Nov 1
 4\, 2026.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/assassins-
 the-musical-19-10-2026-15-37-31
END:VEVENT
