BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Decatur Creek and Patty Keough at Stage 33 Live
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTSTAMP:20261108T170746Z
UID:6be4ef3d314e82bfe24a6e33ad122a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Decatur Creek and Patty Keough split the bill in a 3:00 matine
 e on November 8\, 2026. Tickets are a discounted $15 in advance through st
 age33live.com\, or $20 at the door as available. Advance tickets guarantee
  entry. Only 40 tickets will be sold. All proceeds go to the performers. D
 oug Farrell\, Jack Henry\, and Beth Eldridge — each a talented singer/so
 ngwriter and multi-instrumentalist — banded together to form Decatur Cre
 ek\, blending their solo styles to create an original acoustic sound. Infl
 uences run from traditional and roots Americana to country and folk\, with
  well-crafted songs\, warm vocals with tight harmonies\, and crisp musicia
 nship that flows with rhythm\, soul\, and wit. Decatur Creek is one of the
  region’s real gems. Patty Keough\, after doing time in the corporate mi
 nes\, took to the stage and never looked back. She writes songs that get p
 eople crying… tears of laughter\, or shared sorrow. She lives off-grid i
 n Vermont with farmer friends\, plenty of wine\, and lots of cats. She doe
 s animal rescue — mostly cats\, as they’re 75% of the stray population
  — and she uses all of her performance income\, tips\, and donations in 
 her rescue activities.\n\nSources: Vermont.com\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Stage 33 Live\, 33 Bridge Street\, Bellows Falls VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/decatur-cr
 eek-and-patty-keough-at-stage-33-live-25-10-2026-08-12-15
END:VEVENT
