BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nov. 8 | Hitchcock's 'The Trouble With Harry': Film Screening & Co
 nversation
DTSTART:20261108T140000
DTEND:20261108T170000
DTSTAMP:20261108T170746Z
UID:49fb4f12ef8979931257161be3587c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The screening will be followed by a community conversation led
  by Bess O’Brien\, with Jeanine B. Frost and additional participants to 
 be announced. Presented by On Goldfish Pond Creative as part of Hollywood 
 VT\, and by Latchis Arts\, The Trouble with Harry stars Shirley MacLaine\,
  Edmund Gwenn\, John Forsythe\, Mildred Natwick\, Mildred Dunnock and a yo
 ung Jerry Mathers\, with costumes by eight-time Academy Award winner Edith
  Head. In 2012\, The Guardian’s Peter Bradshaw called it Hitchcock’s 
 “lost masterpiece.” A dead body in the woods of the fictional Vermont 
 town of Highwater is where the trouble begins. Several neighbors suspect t
 hey may be responsible for Harry Worp’s death. Their response\, however
 \, is less panic than practical inconvenience. Harry is buried\, unburied 
 and moved repeatedly while friendship and romance unfold around him.\n\nSo
 urces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Latchis Theater\, 50 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/nov-8-hitc
 hcocks-the-trouble-with-harry-film-screening-amp-conversation-29-09-2026-1
 1-01-35
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Punch Brothers
DTSTART:20261108T190000
DTEND:20261108T210000
DTSTAMP:20261108T170746Z
UID:da50463037434a4fc1fc2e5d37b4b6@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Punch Brothers\, formed by mandolinist Chris Thile in 2006\, i
 s known for pushing the boundaries of acoustic music. In addition to Thile
 \, the band currently comprises guitarist Chris Eldridge\, bassist Paul Ko
 wert\, banjoist Noam Pikelny\, and violinist Brittany Haas. Punch Brothers
  has garnered critical acclaim\, including a Grammy for Best Folk Album fo
 r All Ashore (2018). The Washington Post applauded them for taking “blue
 grass to its next evolutionary stage\, drawing equal inspiration from the 
 brain and the heart.” Over the past two decades\, Punch Brothers has bec
 ome a pioneer in modern string music\, with albums like Antifogmatic (2010
 )\, Who’s Feeling Young Now (2012)\, and The Phosphorescent Blues (2015)
  showcasing the group’s genre-defying sound. Rolling Stone praised their
  work as “wild virtuosity used for more than just virtuosity\,” cement
 ing their reputation as trailblazers in contemporary acoustic music. The b
 and’s most recent album\, Hell on Church Street (2021)\, is a reimaginin
 g of\, and homage to\, the late bluegrass great Tony Rice’s landmark sol
 o album Church Street Blues. Most recently\, Punch Brothers have been focu
 sed on the band’s musical variety show\, The Energy Curfew Music Hour. S
 eason One is available on all podcast platforms\, with season two exclusiv
 ely out on Audible. Season 1 was nominated for a Webby Award in the Podcas
 t: Features\, Experimental & Innovation category\; it also won Most Innova
 tive Audio Experience\, Best Live Podcast Recording\, and Best Sound Desig
 n in the Listener’s Choice category of the 2025 Signal Awards. 30 Center
  St Rutland \, Vermont 05701 802-775-0903 boxoffice@paramountvt.org https:
 //www.paramountvt.org/ Submit An Event Find out what's happening in your n
 eck of the woods with Vermont Public's free Events newsletter. Email Addre
