BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Janus Press: A Maker's Perspective
DTSTART:20261108T160000
DTEND:20261108T170000
DTSTAMP:20261108T170746Z
UID:942070676fa8a1deb70d0b6194904a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Founded by Claire Van Vliet in 1955\, the Janus Press is natio
 nally and internationally known for publishing and producing handmade book
 s on a variety of subjects with a detailed eye for materials and construct
 ion. Since 2004 Andrew Miller-Brown has worked alongside Claire learning a
 nd making at the press. On Sunday\, November 8 at 4pm\, Andrew will presen
 t an overview of the Janus Press and a firsthand look at the creation of t
 hese distinct books. The Craftsbury Public Library was gifted a collection
  of Janus Press works by Paul Gruhler and Jane Marlin in July\, and these 
 books are now on display in the library for all to enjoy. Some of Andrew
 ’s talk will focus on books in the Gruhler collection\, and these books 
 will be available for people to view after the talk. Funding for this talk
  has been provided by Concept 2. For more information\, contact the librar
 y at 802-586-9683. Craftsbury Public Library Artist Group Info director@cr
 aftsburypubliclibrary.org Craftsbury Public Library 149 Common Loop Crafts
 bury COmmon \, Vermont 05827 802-586-9683 director@craftsburypubliclibrary
